# Store profile for a storefront in the Hydrogen sales channel.
# 1. Copy to envs/<store>.env and fill in PUBLIC_STORE_DOMAIN.
# 2. Link the project to the storefront once: `npx shopify hydrogen link`.
# 3. Run `STORE=<store> npm run dev`.
#
# The Storefront API tokens, the Customer Account API credentials and SESSION_SECRET come
# from the linked storefront (Hydrogen → your storefront → Environments and variables),
# and `npm run dev` registers the customer login tunnel with it. A variable set in this
# file overrides the linked one, even when it is empty.
# Required variables are set; uncomment an optional one to use it.

SALES_CHANNEL="hydrogen"

# Required. The store's permanent *.myshopify.com domain. It has to match the linked store.
PUBLIC_STORE_DOMAIN=""

# Optional. Domain the checkout runs on, usually the primary domain. The linked storefront
# doesn't provide it; set it here or in the storefront's environment variables.
# PUBLIC_CHECKOUT_DOMAIN=""

# Optional. Growave admin → Settings → API. Server-only; signs logged-in customers for
# Growave. You can also add it to the storefront's environment variables as a secret.
# PRIVATE_GROWAVE_API_SECRET=""

# Optional. Growave admin → Instagram → gallery ID. Without it the galleries are hidden.
# PUBLIC_GROWAVE_INSTAGRAM_GALLERY_ID=""
